<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emanuel Merck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1794">1794</a>–<a href="/years/1855">1855</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Heinrich Emanuel Merck</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emanuel Merck was a German pharmacist who turned his family's pharmacy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> into an industrial firm. From 1827 he began manufacturing alkaloids such as morphine on a large scale for doctors and pharmacists. The company, Merck, became one of the world's leading chemical and pharmaceutical businesses and is still based in Darmstadt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emanuel-merck.jpg" alt="Emanuel Merck" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:E_MERCK_PAINT_LON.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
